  "answer": "The advertised support for precise PDF citations needs qualification: PDF citation accuracy is highly dependent on document quality. Scanned, photocopied, or image-only PDFs lack native text layers and require OCR processing; low-quality scans or complex layouts can produce broken text blocks, causing missing citations, incorrect page links, or the assistant failing to find answers that actually exist [NL-002#NL-002-S09]. Even with OCR, blurry or low-resolution scans may result in broken citations and gaps in knowledge [NL-006#NL-006-S03]. The remaining support tickets after the April fix were almost entirely tied to scanned, image-only PDFs, where TutorChat often links to the start of the file rather than the specific page [NL-011#NL-011-S05]. The recommended nuance is that fully reliable PDF citations apply mainly to natively digital, text-searchable PDFs; scanned documents should be converted to structured digital formats prior to upload [NL-002#NL-002-S09].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
